WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.472
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 4: Inventions and Creativity.

2
00:00:04.552 --> 00:00:12.915
This unit is all about inventions and creativity — two
powerful forces that have shaped the world we live in today.

3
00:00:12.995 --> 00:00:20.184
Throughout history, people have looked at problems
around them and imagined new ways to solve them.

4
00:00:20.264 --> 00:00:28.774
From the simple wheel to the complex machines of the modern
age, every invention began as an idea in somebody’s mind.

5
00:00:28.854 --> 00:00:35.675
In this unit, you will explore how inventions
work, why they matter, and how ordinary people —

6
00:00:35.755 --> 00:00:41.916
including young people just like you — have
changed the world with creative thinking.

7
00:00:41.996 --> 00:00:48.083
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:48.163 --> 00:00:55.563
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use
vocabulary related to inventions, exploration, science,

9
00:00:55.643 --> 00:00:59.087
and technology confidently in speech and writing.

10
00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:07.717
You will also read and understand an informational passage
about inventions and answer comprehension questions about it.

11
00:01:07.797 --> 00:01:14.405
You will also identify the past simple tense
in sentences and explain when and why we use it.

12
00:01:14.485 --> 00:01:17.066
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:17.146 --> 00:01:23.789
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: straits,
explorer, excursion, caravan, territory, navigation.

14
00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:28.878
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:32.837
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:39.706
The reading sequence includes Inventions That Changed
Everyday Life and A Gadget You Could Build: The SunJar.

17
00:01:39.786 --> 00:01:40.588
Read actively.

18
00:01:40.668 --> 00:01:44.937
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:49.033
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:49.113 --> 00:01:53.094
The first language focus is Past Simple Tense (Reviewed).

21
00:01:53.174 --> 00:02:00.646
The past simple tense describes actions that happened
at a definite time in the past and are now finished,

22
00:02:00.726 --> 00:02:05.562
which is why we use it when we talk
about inventions and discoveries.

23
00:02:05.642 --> 00:02:13.328
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:13.408 --> 00:02:17.719
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Present Your Invention.

25
00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:22.178
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:22.258 --> 00:02:25.571
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:25.651 --> 00:02:29.098
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:29.178 --> 00:02:30.795
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:30.875 --> 00:02:38.101
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:38.181 --> 00:02:41.644
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:41.724 --> 00:02:49.983
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
